 "title": "The sphere's count needs polynomial-calculus degree n^{Omega(1)} over every field",
 "subject": "The knot sphere's contradiction (the Kasteleyn-signed NAE formula of the octahedral sphere) in proof complexity",
 "conclusion": "Over every field, every polynomial-calculus refutation of the octahedral knot sphere's count has degree at least c n^{1/4}/log n, because a low-degree refutation would give one for the functional pigeonhole principle on an expander. Over F2, tree-like Res(xor) refutations of the count therefore need size 2^{Omega(n^{1/4}/log n)}.",
